    "rationale": "Per banking convention articulated by Joshua: Branch performance = Branch Manager's performance, Area Manager BSC = aggregate of branches reporting to them, Head of Branches BSC = aggregate of Area Managers, Chief Retail BSC = aggregate of Head of Branches. Senior BMs run flagship branches but don't supervise other BMs."
  },
  "profitability_axis": {
    "_doc": "v10.374 \u2014 Profitability axis for every role. Complementary to role_tiers (seniority). Five tiers: portfolio_owner (tagged to customers via accounts.csv::relationship_manager_code, drives sales \u2014 includes Branch sales like RM PB/BB/DSO/BRM/SRO/RO + HO sales like Sector Specialists/HO Corporate/SME/Sector RMs reporting to Chief Commercial); proposition_owner (owns an overlapping proposition like Women Banking/Diaspora \u2014 NOT tagged to accounts, responsible for proposition growth; per Rule 6, propositions overlap by design); structural_owner (owns PBT at structural level via the branch_pbt_allocator or higher rollup \u2014 NOT tagged to accounts \u2014 includes Branch Manager, Regional Head, Heads of business lines, Directors, MD); service (operational branch role; occasionally tagged when introducing accounts but not primary sales \u2014 Teller, CSO, BOS); support (head office support function \u2014 Risk/Compliance/IT/HR/Finance/Audit \u2014 owns cost center but not direct PBT). Each role also has branch_scope (branch_bound / head_office / national) and optional sbu mapping (Retail Banking / Commercial Banking / Corporate Banking / Treasury / Digital_Agency / Support / Executive).",
